==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|rupture|lang=fr}}, or its source, {{etyl|la}} {{term|ruptura||a breaking, rupture (of a limb or vein), in {{etyl|ML.}} also a road, a field, a form of feudal tenure, a tax, etc.}}, from the participle stem of {{term|rumpere||to break, burst}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈɹʌptʃə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[burst]], [[split]], or [[break]].
# A social [[breach]] or [[break]], between individuals or groups.
# {{medicine}} A break or tear in [[soft tissue]], such as a [[muscle]].
# {{engineering}} A [[failure]] mode in which a tough [[ductile]] material pulls apart rather than cracking.

